\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {6.3}{\ignorespaces Statistics of the Acrobot trajectory optimization using the \textbf  {Full SELF} sparsity setting (complete stage-wise cliques $I_k$) for desired absolute rotations of both links. The terminal rotation error is defined as $e_R(T) = \left ( \DOTSB \sum@ \slimits@ _{i=1}^{2} \left \|R_{i,N}-R_{i,\mathrm  {des}}\right \|_F^2 \right )^{1/2}$. The maximum manifold violation is $\varepsilon _{\mathrm  {SO(2)}}^{\max } = \max _{i,k,X\in \{R,F\}} \|X_{i,k}^{\top }X_{i,k}-I_2\|_F$. For each moment block $j$, $\delta _j$ denotes its normalized second eigenvalue weight. Thus, $\delta _{\max }=\max _j\delta _j$, while $\delta _{\mathrm  {first}}$ is evaluated for the first moment block. All trajectory metrics use the ordered extraction, and the runtime is the solver operation time.}}{67}{table.caption.49}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:acrobot_sdp_statistics_full}{{6.3}{67}{Statistics of the Acrobot trajectory optimization using the \textbf {Full SELF} sparsity setting (complete stage-wise cliques $I_k$) for desired absolute rotations of both links. The terminal rotation error is defined as $e_R(T) = \left ( \sum _{i=1}^{2} \left \|R_{i,N}-R_{i,\mathrm {des}}\right \|_F^2 \right )^{1/2}$. The maximum manifold violation is $\varepsilon _{\mathrm {SO(2)}}^{\max } = \max _{i,k,X\in \{R,F\}} \|X_{i,k}^{\top }X_{i,k}-I_2\|_F$. For each moment block $j$, $\delta _j$ denotes its normalized second eigenvalue weight. Thus, $\delta _{\max }=\max _j\delta _j$, while $\delta _{\mathrm {first}}$ is evaluated for the first moment block. All trajectory metrics use the ordered extraction, and the runtime is the solver operation time}{table.caption.49}{}}
